Amix: the SDK host API over the kernel's zz9ksvc channel (ZZ9K_HOST_AMIX).

On Amix the kernel module zz9ksvc owns the board's mailbox, so the host code cannot write
the rings itself.  With ZZ9K_HOST_AMIX (the build sets it) a context is an open of
/dev/zz9ksvcN: zz9k_call submits by ZZSIOC_SUBMIT and waits by ZZSIOC_WAIT (the kernel
gives the request its id and swaps the open's handles for the runtime's), zz9k_alloc_shared
is ZZSIOC_ALLOC and an mmap(2) of the cookie, zz9k_free_shared unmaps exactly what was
mapped and frees, zz9k_close unmaps everything before it closes.  zz9k_open takes the first
unit that answers and zz9k_open_unit (zz9k/amix.h) a given one.  The raw ring calls
(zz9k_submit, zz9k_poll) and the interrupt calls answer ZZ9K_STATUS_UNSUPPORTED, as on any
host without a mailbox; the kernel polls.  Upstream lines are only added to, except the
platform test's #if, which becomes an #elif after the new branch.

